<title>INDIA: Indian exports rose 6.0 pct in July.</title>
<headline>Indian exports rose 6.0 pct in July.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian merchandise exports increased to $2.60 billion in July, up 6.0 percent from $2.45 billion in the same month in 1995, the government said on Friday.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Jul 96    Jun 96    Jul 95</p>
<p>    Exports		  2.60	2.59	2.45</p>
<p>    Imports		  2.73	2.81	3.02</p>
<p>    Trade balance	 -0.13     -0.21     -0.56</p>
<p>Note - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.  </p>
<p>Indian merchandise exports grew 11.45 percent in the four-month period between April and July to $10.84 billion, compared to $9.72 billion in the same period in 1995, the statement said.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   Apr-July 1996     Apr-July 1995</p>
<p>    Exports		     10.84		 9.72</p>
<p>    Imports		     11.92		11.25</p>
<p>    Trade balance	     -1.08		-1.53</p>
<p>Note - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.</p>
</text>
